      {
        "id": 235700,
        "name": "Jonas Ståleker",
        "username": "JoeSteeloak",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/joesteeloak/{size}/4853_2.png",
        "created_at": "2021-03-06T09:37:38.020Z",
        "cooked": "<p>So many to choose from! It all depends on how you want the hero to play. I will give you an example from each category, but I honestly think you could go with literally any of them.</p>\n<p>Background: <strong>Former Villain</strong>, this ties into Magneto once being a villain, but is now a hero.</p>\n<p>Power source: <strong>Accident</strong>, pick up <strong>Metal</strong> as a Materials Power of course. The ability <strong>Inflict</strong> could be the hero wrapping up people in metal (both hindering and damaging them)</p>\n<p>Archetype: <strong>Robot/Cyborg</strong>, but instead of being a robot it is just you controlling metal around you. <strong>Metal Skin</strong> represents either deflecting bullets with magnetism or floating metal plates around you at all times.</p>\n<p>Background: <strong>Analytical</strong>, someone surrounded by metal all the time might be a bit cold and calculating perhaps.</p>\n<p>Red Abilities: <strong>Field of Hazards</strong> (Materials Powers), just crunch up all metal in the scene, maybe even turning them into caltrops on the ground.</p>\n<p>Also choose <strong>Purification</strong> (Mental Qualities), just get rid of all metal in the scene.</p>\n<p>Hope this gives some inspiration. Knowing more <strong>how</strong> the Magneto like character would use its powers would probably make it easier to create the hero.</p>",
        "post_number": 2,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-03-06T09:39:02.397Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
